        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Separate components: the level anchor is June's Initial total. Momentum moderates the decline because the last three initial-print changes average -0.315185 million. No separately quantified one-off adjustment is applied. USDA's implementation memo expands the time-limit population from ages 18-54 to 18-64 and narrows the dependent-child exception to children under 14, supporting continued recertification losses. California's official guidance begins implementation in June 2026 and prohibits countable months before June, limiting the case for a broad California duration cutoff in July. Policy effects are represented through the observed drift and interval uncertainty rather than an additional unmeasured enrollment deduction."
