        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use a June-level persistence prior with drift estimated from seven Initial prints spanning December 2025-June 2026. The six changes, in millions, are -0.965303, -0.676913, -0.572546, -0.287175, -0.448968, and -0.209412. Their mean is -0.5267195; the last-three mean is -0.315185. Equal weighting gives forecast drift -0.42095225, equivalent to a +0.10576725 momentum update to the drift prior; separate one-off and additional policy adjustments are zero. sigma = 0.276088593 million, computed as sqrt(0.3811245548055 / 5). The normal-approximation 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 0.353393399 million. Multiply that width by 1.25 for the small historical sample, staggered policy implementation, and demonstrated initial-reporting variability, giving 0.441741748 million. The implied point is 35.93176375 and bounds are 35.490022002-36.373505498 million; emitted values are rounded to six decimals."
